# VietLaw Limited Demo — Cloudflare Pages production build variables.
#
# Vite embeds every `VITE_*` variable into the built JS bundle AT BUILD
# TIME (see https://vite.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html) -- it is not read at
# runtime and is not a secret store. Do not put an API key or any backend
# secret in a `VITE_*` variable: whatever value is set here becomes
# plainly visible in the shipped, unminified-readable bundle to anyone who
# opens browser devtools.
#
# Copy this file's variable names into the Cloudflare Pages dashboard
# (Settings -> Environment variables -> Production), with the REAL
# Railway backend URL as the value. Do not commit a real `.env.production`.

# The Railway backend's public HTTPS URL (generated once the Railway
# service exists -- see DEPLOY_RAILWAY_CLOUDFLARE.md). Must be the exact
# origin (scheme + host), no trailing slash, no path.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://<your-railway-service>.up.railway.app
